# Undergraduate Chemical Engineering Curricular Architecture
#
# ABET-accredited Bachelor of Science (B.S.) in Chemical Engineering: transport phenomena, reactor design, separations, and process control.

#>spw_cache_univ_undergrad_cheme
#:cache #!chemical_engineering
#:layer #!pragmatics

^"intent"{
  ~#goal: "Model the four-year undergraduate curriculum for an ABET-accredited Bachelor of Science in Chemical Engineering, articulating conservation laws, unit operations, reaction kinetics, and plant design."
  ~#accreditation: "ABET Engineering Accreditation Commission (EAC) Criteria for Chemical Engineering"
}

^["material_and_energy_balances"]{
  gateway_course: "Introduction to Chemical Engineering Analysis."
  foundations: #[
    "Macroscopic Conservation Laws: Differential and integral mass and species balances for steady and unsteady state systems",
    "Degrees of Freedom Analysis: Systematic determination of mathematical well-posedness for complex flowsheets",
    "Recycle, Bypass, and Purge Streams: Governing steady-state accumulation of inerts and unconverted reactants",
    "First Law of Thermodynamics: Open and closed system energy balances, sensible heat, latent phase change enthalpies, and heats of formation",
    "Combustion & Psychrometry: Theoretical air calculations, flue gas analysis, wet/dry bulb temperatures, and humidity charts"
  ]
}

^["transport_phenomena_fluid_heat_and_mass"]{
  engineering_core: "Momentum, Heat, and Mass Transfer sequence."
  transport_branches: .{
    fluid_mechanics: #[
      "Differential momentum balances: Continuity and Navier-Stokes equations in Cartesian and cylindrical coordinates",
      "Friction factors and head loss: Moody chart, Darcy-Weisbach equation, and minor losses in piping networks",
      "Pumping and compression: Net Positive Suction Head (NPSH), centrifugal pump curves, and cavitation avoidance",
      "Fluidization & porous media: Ergun equation for packed beds and minimum fluidization velocity"
    ]
    heat_transfer: #[
      "Conduction: Fourier's law, 1D/2D steady-state conduction, and transient heat transfer with low/high Biot numbers",
      "Convection: Forced and natural convection correlations (Nusselt, Reynolds, and Prandtl dimensionless numbers)",
      "Heat Exchanger Design: Log-Mean Temperature Difference (LMTD) method and Effectiveness-NTU design for shell-and-tube exchangers",
      "Radiative Exchange: Stefan-Boltzmann law, surface emissivity, and view factor geometry"
    ]
    mass_transfer: #[
      "Molecular Diffusion: Fick's first and second laws, equimolar counterdiffusion, and diffusion through stagnant films",
      "Convective Mass Transfer: Interphase mass transfer film theory, Sherwood and Schmidt numbers, and two-resistance theory"
    ]
  }[reg=facet]
}

^["chemical_reaction_engineering"]{
  junior_core: "Kinetics and Chemical Reactor Design."
  reactor_paradigms: #[
    "Ideal Reactor Archetypes: Sizing equations for Batch Reactors, Continuous Stirred-Tank Reactors (CSTR), and Plug Flow Reactors (PFR)",
    "Reactor Networks: Optimizing conversion and selectivity for parallel and series reaction networks via recycle and staged feed",
    "Non-Isothermal Operations: Energy balance coupling, heat generation vs cooling curves, and thermal runaway runaway criteria",
    "Heterogeneous Catalysis Fundamentals: Langmuir-Hinshelwood rate laws, internal pore diffusion, effectiveness factors, and Thiele modulus",
    "Residence Time Distribution (RTD): Pulse/step tracer experiments, E(t) curves, and non-ideal dispersion/segregation models"
  ]
}

^["equilibrium_staged_separations"]{
  junior_core: "Mass Transfer Operations and Separation Processes."
  separation_technologies: .{
    distillation_systems: "Vapor-liquid equilibria (VLE), Raoult's law, relative volatility, McCabe-Thiele graphical method, and reflux ratio optimization"
    multicomponent_distillation: "Fenske-Underwood-Gilliland shortcut equations for light/heavy key components and rigorous tray-by-tray column simulation"
    absorption_and_stripping: "Packed tower absorption, Henry's law, Height of a Transfer Unit (HTU), and Number of Transfer Units (NTU)"
    liquid_liquid_extraction: "Ternary liquid equilibria phase diagrams, tie lines, partition coefficients, and countercurrent extraction stages"
    membrane_separations: "Reverse osmosis, ultrafiltration, gas permeation, and crossflow concentration polarization modeling"
  }[reg=facet]
}

^["process_dynamics_and_control"]{
  senior_core: "Chemical Process Dynamics and Automated Control."
  control_systems: #[
    "Dynamic Modeling & Laplace Transforms: Transfer functions for first-order plus dead time (FOPDT) and second-order chemical processes",
    "Feedback Control Architecture: Proportional-Integral-Derivative (PID) controllers and industrial loop tuning (Ziegler-Nichols, Cohen-Coon, IMC)",
    "Frequency Response & Stability: Bode plots, Nyquist stability criterion, gain and phase margins, and Routh-Hurwitz array testing",
    "Advanced Control Strategies: Feedforward control, cascade loops, ratio control, and dead-time compensation (Smith Predictor)"
  ]
}

^["senior_capstone_plant_design_and_process_safety"]{
  senior_culmination: "Two-semester Chemical Process Plant Design and Unit Operations Laboratory."
  plant_engineering_deliverables: #[
    "Process Flowsheeting: ASPEN Plus or HYSYS steady-state plant simulation, thermodynamic property method selection, and stream convergence",
    "Economic Evaluation: Capital expenditure (CAPEX) via Guthrie module factors, operating costs (OPEX), discounted cash flow, Net Present Value (NPV), and Payback Period",
    "Process Safety Management (OSHA PSM): Hazard and Operability Studies (HAZOP), Layer of Protection Analysis (LOPA), and emergency pressure relief valve sizing",
    "Unit Operations Lab Practicum: Operation of pilot-scale fractional distillation columns, packed absorption towers, and pilot tubular reactors"
  ]
}

^["taste"]{
  ~#taste: "Chemical engineering is the discipline that bends physical chemistry to the service of human scale, transforming beaker reactions into continuous industrial reality."
  ~#wonder: "Why does an apparently modest increase in pipe diameter cut the pumping energy consumption by the fifth power of the radius?"

  principles: #[
    "Conservation is absolute: Mass and energy balances must close to zero; you cannot negotiate with the laws of thermodynamics.",
    "Scale reveals demons: A reaction that behaves meekly in a 100 mL flask can explode catastrophically when scaled to a 5,000-gallon batch due to surface-area-to-volume heat transfer limits.",
    "Process safety is moral stewardship: Every valve, interlock, and rupture disk is an ethical commitment to the lives of plant workers and surrounding communities."
  ]
}

^"invariants"{
  "Senior capstone projects must pass a formal HAZOP process safety evaluation prior to final design approval.",
  "Unit operations laboratory experiments require pre-lab safety walkthroughs and verified interlock functionality.",
  "All chemical engineering graduates must demonstrate proficiency in continuous process flowsheeting software (e.g., ASPEN Plus or HYSYS).",
}

#>wonder_undergrad_cheme_1
?["How does the introduction of dynamic digital twin simulations in process control labs alter student response time during simulated chemical runaway crises?"]{
  #:depth #!pedagogical ~#lens(plant_safety_simulation)
  ~#hypothesis: "Undergraduates trained on interactive high-fidelity process simulators (simulating exothermic runaway in CSTRs) diagnose sensor failures and execute safe emergency shutdown 50% faster during capstone operations."
  !probe{ "Measure mean time to safe shutdown (MTSS) and alarm acknowledgment accuracy in senior design teams facing unexpected cooling jacket pump failures." }
  $%[safety.mean_time_to_shutdown_seconds, control.alarm_mitigation_accuracy]
}
